{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbvNn1fUUDgmbwthpm52","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RojJBZs9MG83xdAJUKHjAC","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"picked":3,"why":"Take 3 has the most life: money arriving first makes a much-burned driver suspicious, and that drives the demand for exact terms. I applied the review's fixes except its cut of the send-off. Route B has the turned driver warn the rivals' lookout off [dd8b9b4144cb97176295edbd, 824dc977c7edf50d72a1db3e], and the scene sheet requires the offer. For Aster: the review treats this send-off as the Scout's false tip, and that needs correcting or a ruling from Sky.","changes":["Line 1: dropped the figure as the review asked, because the scene sheet gives no price. The review's reason is off: §07 prices the driver at Pay $70,000 or Help $40,000 [dd8b9b4144cb97176295edbd, 824dc977c7edf50d72a1db3e], while the purse and people rules use $40,000 [cd8c0574c7d27811e99467f1, ab8f73121466f6e810b67979], apparently the Help price. Aster should confirm.","Line 8: now \"The back seat's our business\", as the review asked. It says nothing about how the Take goes, so it holds for both the built and the decided versions [12f568e600e22c6cfd665124]. The review's reason is only partly right: the human GDD still has the Enforcer taking Vale from the back seat [dd8b9b4144cb97176295edbd].","Line 9: dropped \"free\", since nothing sets that price, but did not make the requested cut to \"I don't see that.\" The send-off is the driver warning the rivals' lookout off, which is in route B and separate from the Scout's false tip, the part in question [dd8b9b4144cb97176295edbd]. Cutting it would also drop a line the sheet requires."],"beats":[{"speaker":"Zhou","line":"Paid, and I haven't heard the job. Nobody pays first."},{"speaker":"Fixer","line":"We do. We hear the Councillor's driver has had a lean month."},{"speaker":"Zhou","line":"I don't ask who \"we\" is. Last time, the money stopped."},{"speaker":"Fixer","line":"Then you're the only honest person on Apron Road, Zhou."},{"speaker":"Zhou","line":"Honest is extra. I've been paid for \"small favours\", so what, exactly?"},{"speaker":"Fixer","line":"At the chime, take the Councillor to the service bay. Not home."},{"speaker":"Zhou","line":"East yard. A couple of minutes, then I drive on."},{"speaker":"Fixer","line":"Long enough. The back seat's our business."},{"speaker":"Zhou","line":"I don't see that. Anyone watching my bay, I'll send off."}],"learned":["Paid: Vale's car waits out back."],"opens":["Be at the service bay"]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8483,"cache_read_input_tokens":4596,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8483},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b1a82a92-bae9-4673-a906-aeb730fda73f","uuid":"c7ca5682-9aa7-4a44-b767-3565ef9571e6","timestamp":"2026-11-01T08:50:38.296Z","request_id":"req_011CgbvNmk3afmgq8RsS8S52","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01RojJBZs9MG83xdAJUKHjAC":{"picked":3,"why":"Take 3 has the most life: money arriving first makes a much-burned driver suspicious, and that drives the demand for exact terms. I applied the review's fixes except its cut of the send-off. Route B has the turned driver warn the rivals' lookout off [dd8b9b4144cb97176295edbd, 824dc977c7edf50d72a1db3e], and the scene sheet requires the offer. For Aster: the review treats this send-off as the Scout's false tip, and that needs correcting or a ruling from Sky.","changes":["Line 1: dropped the figure as the review asked, because the scene sheet gives no price. The review's reason is off: §07 prices the driver at Pay $70,000 or Help $40,000 [d